stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> ACTIVE: E1 authored on a synthetic tenant, expectations produced by the engine, second-person review
    ACTIVE --> REDERIVE_PENDING: E2 a pinned rule, ledger fixture or corpus version is superseded for the case period
    REDERIVE_PENDING --> ACTIVE: E3 engine re-run and any changed expectation reviewed with a reason
    ACTIVE --> RETIRED: E4 use case retired or case superseded
    REDERIVE_PENDING --> RETIRED: E4 use case retired or case superseded
    RETIRED --> [*]

    note right of REDERIVE_PENDING
      Blocks the release gate for its use case,
      not live traffic. Live answers are still
      checked against the engine at runtime.
    end note
